# Docker runtime

- `internal/docker.Client` is the only code that runs `docker`. It takes an injectable `Runner` (real: `ExecRunner`; tests: `internal/docker/dockertest.Fake`, an in-memory CLI that records argv and child env). No shell, a timeout on every call (follow logs are bounded by ctx), `--` before positional arguments, `--format '{{json .}}'`/inspect JSON instead of text parsing. The child gets a minimal allowlisted environment (`BaseEnv`), never the daemon's.
- Every created object carries `LabelManaged=true` (plus `server-id`, `server`, `project-id`, `config-hash` on containers). Containers are reachable only through server-id lookups (`ServerContainers`, `StopServer`, `RemoveServerContainers`, `ServerLogs`, `ServerStats`); no method takes a client-supplied container name or id. Labels are filtered by Docker **and** re-checked on the inspected object. Image/volume removal inspects and verifies the label, refuses objects used by any container (`ErrInUse`), and an unmanaged `golem-deploy` network is refused, not joined. Keep tests that prove an unmanaged object gets no destructive argv.
- Env values never appear in argv, logs or errors: `RunSpec.Args` emits `--env KEY` and returns `KEY=value` for the child environment. Env keys that would steer the CLI child (`DOCKER_*`, `PATH`, `HOME`, proxies, Windows system variables) are reserved.
- `RunSpec` applies the hardening on every run; its extension fields (`DaemonEnv`, `ReadOnlyBinds`, `DataVolume`, `AdminPort`, `GID`) are for the build/engine milestone. Change hardening flags only with the exact-argv test in `client_test.go` and `docs/SERVERS.md`.
- Errors are `*CmdError` wrapping a sentinel (`ErrUnavailable`, `ErrNotFound`, `ErrConflict`, `ErrPortBusy`, ...); its `Detail` (CLI stderr) may go to daemon and job logs, never to HTTP responses. `Reachable` caches the `docker version` probe for `GET /status`.
- `internal/ports` validates `--port-range` (1024 ≤ range < 32768, not containing the panel port, browser-unsafe ports skipped), picks the lowest free port and probes the host (TCP+UDP bind).
- Verify with `go test ./internal/docker/... ./internal/ports/...`; with Docker available also `GOLEM_DEPLOY_DOCKER_TESTS=1 go test ./internal/docker/... ./internal/httpapi/...` (builds images from a digest-pinned busybox, cleans up; CI does not run it).
